WEBVTT

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:03.420
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:06.560
Vanish, Cyberse!

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.890
Track him down.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:23.680
Only that Ignis knows the Cyberse's location!

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:28.620
SOL Technologies is the long-time 
leader of the network.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:33.420
But five years ago, due to Hanoi's attacks...

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:37.750
...the AI known as Ignis hid the 
Cyberse somewhere in the network.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:43.520
We must do whatever it takes to find that 
Ignis and learn the location of the Cyberse.

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:47.330
It seems SOL Technologies 
is looking for something.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:51.700
Not just SOL Technologies.  The 
Knights of Hanoi are after it too.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:55.830
If I capture the AI, it'll be 
my secret weapon against Hanoi.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:58.300
This program is the Knights of Hanoi!

00:00:58.520 --> 00:00:59.620
What?

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:03.650
I'll crush anyone who gets in my way!

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:05.500
Come to me!

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.820
Welcome.  You're going to be our savior.

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:13.000
What?  I'm captured?

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:16.990
Deck set!  Into the VRAINS!

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.100
Who are you?

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:26.570
My name is Playmaker!

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:29.670
I have what you're looking for.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:33.870
If you want it, you have 
to defeat me in a duel.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.360
Seize the wind, Playmaker!

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:40.750
Here we go!  Speed Duel!

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:59.760
I run Across the universe

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:02.930
At the speed of light

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:04.800
Begin Loading

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.530
Open the door of dreams

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:12.100
VRAINS spreads

00:02:12.350 --> 00:02:15.210
Believe in myself

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:18.740
VRAINS continues

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:24.050
The circuit draws the future

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:28.120
I'll grab it with my own hands  Yeah

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:29.720
Access!

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:32.420
Start swirling, Data Storm!

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.030
I'm now With the Wind

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:36.330
Link with my soul

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:39.100
Speed up, Data Storm!

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:40.830
Now Win the Race

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:43.670
Connected world

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:47.170
No matter when

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:50.540
Nothing is impossible

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:54.680
Strive for hope

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:59.250
And ride the wind!

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:15.740
The Ignis...

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.680
He captured it?

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:35.460
This wind...  This is a Speed Duel?

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:41.700
Playmaker, do you know the differences 
between a Speed Duel and a Master Duel?

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:43.650
Explain.  But keep it short.

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:45.820
You don't need to be so arrogant.

00:03:45.820 --> 00:03:48.710
Don't forget that you're a hostage.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:51.180
Yeah yeah.  I'll keep it short.

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:57.880
The first difference is that there are three 
Main Monster Zones and Spell/Trap Zones.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.340
Three?

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:03.690
Is there a three Main Monster Zone limit?

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:07.660
I already know about Speed Duels?

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:10.460
Your start with four cards in your hand.

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:12.120
And there's no Main Phase 2.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.720
It's simpler than a Master Duel.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.100
Exactly.

00:04:23.420 --> 00:04:26.180
Speed Duel, huh?  Interesting.

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:30.050
It seems he knows about Speed Duels.

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:32.600
In that case, shall I help you?

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:33.670
No need.

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:36.830
I want to live too, you know.

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:38.840
I'm not comfortable letting you-

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:40.930
Be quiet!  I need to focus!

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:41.860
Yeah yeah.

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:43.090
Let's go!

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:46.770
Speed Duel!

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:54.380
He's capturing the spotlight more than me!

00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:07.650
What's this duel?

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:10.000
It's called a Speed Duel.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:12.100
Speed Duel?

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:14.990
I heard rumors about it before.

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:18.070
Yeah.  A duel where you ride the wind.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.300
Speed Duel...

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:24.100
I'm counting on you, Yusaku.

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:26.970
I'll go first.

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:28.660
My turn!

00:05:28.950 --> 00:05:31.100
A perfect hand.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:34.250
I can go all out from the start.

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:37.200
I Special Summon Hack Worm.

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:43.390
I can Special Summon it from my hand when 
there are no monsters on your field.

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:46.540
Special Summon for only 400 ATK...

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:49.130
You're planning to summon 
a high Level monster.

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:50.650
Exactly!

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:54.270
I Special Summon another Hack Worm.

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:57.880
This is bad.

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:00.070
I bet he's going to bring out...

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:05.320
Witness the most powerful 
monster that Revolver gave me.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:12.120
Playmaker!  Your hero 
act will come to an end!

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:16.490
I tribute two Hack Worms to Tribute Summon!

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:19.220
Appear, Cracking Dragon!

00:06:26.230 --> 00:06:28.670
I end my turn.

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:31.570
Oh my!  It already showed up!

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:34.180
3000 ATK on the first turn.

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:36.410
What should I do?

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:39.840
Hey!  Playmaker!

00:06:40.070 --> 00:06:41.110
Be quiet!

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:42.750
Look ahead!  Ahead!

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:01.370
Don't let your guard down.

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:05.320
In a Speed Duel, there are 
obstacles other than the duel.

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:08.080
If you take too much damage...

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:11.280
...you'll suffer flashbacks when 
returning from LINK VRAINS...

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:13.010
...and take psychological damage.

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:16.300
You said I couldn't win with this deck.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:18.750
Because of that monster.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.220
You finally understand.

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:29.260
Getting out of this situation 
depends on this draw.

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:37.760
My turn!

00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:40.610
I draw!

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:42.540
Good!  This'll work!

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:44.300
Proceed with caution.

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:47.680
I know.  I set two cards.

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:52.820
I summon Cyberse Wizard!

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:01.080
That's Cyberse-Type!

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:03.600
How can Playmaker have that?

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:10.310
We spent years getting rid of Cyberse 
users, but there's still one left?

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:12.580
Cyberse-Type?

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:14.050
What's that?

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:17.250
I've never seen that Monster Type before.

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:21.210
You use Cyberse?  How unexpected.

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:24.720
But it's powerless against Cracking Dragon!

00:08:25.220 --> 00:08:27.150
My monster's effect activates!

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:33.960
When you summon or Special Summon a monster 
this turn, it loses 200 ATK per Level.

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:37.360
And you take that amount as damage!

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:39.060
Crack Fall!

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:49.310
He lowered Cyberse Wizard's ATK.

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:52.240
But I activate his effect!

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:56.480
Your monster switches to defense 
position once per turn.

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:58.720
Cyberse Algorithm!

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:09.890
When Cyberse Wizard uses his effect...

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:14.600
...Cyberses deal piercing damage 
when they attack this turn.

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:15.830
Battle!

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:18.080
Illusion Spike!

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:26.000
He did it!  Playmaker 
destroyed Hanoi's Dragon!

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:36.190
Cracking Dragon can't be destroyed in battle 
against a monster with equal or lower Level!

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:39.300
Whoa!  I didn't know it had that effect!

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:41.090
Has our enemy improved too?

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:44.820
I see.

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:47.930
Playmaker, you don't seem surprised.

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:52.200
He wasn't worried about 
Cyberse Wizard's effect.

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:54.410
So I figured something was up.

00:09:54.410 --> 00:09:58.880
Ooh.  So you're aware of your 
opponent's tiniest reactions.

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:01.130
I end my turn!

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:04.640
Cracking Dragon's effect ends.

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:11.200
3000 ATK and can't be destroyed 
by Level 8 or lower monsters?

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:13.320
It's too strong!

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:16.240
Do something, Yusaku!

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:18.960
My turn!

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:22.080
This is the crucial moment in the duel.

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:24.500
I activate my Skill!

00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:25.920
Skill?

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:27.860
You told me to keep it short.

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:29.840
So I left that part out.

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:34.580
You oughta think about your 
future a bit more seriously.

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:36.820
I am thinking about it!

00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:42.250
In a Speed Duel, there's a special 
rule that can be used once per duel.

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:43.800
It's called a Skill.

00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:49.560
It can power up your draw, increase 
your LP or your monster's ATK...

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:52.030
There are many different types.

00:10:53.080 --> 00:10:56.000
I activate my Skill, Double Draw!

00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:57.080
No way!

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:59.000
I don't know that Skill!

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:01.970
Hanoi must have created that program!

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:05.140
Excellent.

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:08.500
My strategies are even more perfect.

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:12.300
I activate the spell card, <i>DDoS Attack</i>!

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:20.880
Due to its effect, I send two <i>DDoS 
Attack</i> in my deck to the graveyard.

00:11:23.860 --> 00:11:26.760
For every card I sent to the graveyard...

00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:32.010
...you take damage equal to my 
Machine monster's Level times 100.

00:11:59.980 --> 00:12:03.100
Playmaker, now we're even.

00:12:05.260 --> 00:12:07.480
Nice, Playmaker!

00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:12.040
Don't lose against Hanoi!  
Protect LINK VRAINS!

00:12:12.260 --> 00:12:14.640
I told you - don't let your guard down.

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:18.820
If you take too much damage and 
hit the ground, you'll die!

00:12:18.820 --> 00:12:22.430
You barely survived.  How lucky.

00:12:24.030 --> 00:12:25.530
What's that?

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:40.640
The Data Storm is unstable.

00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:43.370
So it's dangerous.

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:46.020
But inside is...

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:59.020
I set a card and switch Cracking 
Dragon to attack position.

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:06.440
Next, I equip Air Cracking 
Storm on Cracking Dragon!

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:12.770
When the equipped monster 
destroys a monster in battle...

00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:16.430
...the equipped monster can attack again.

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:20.960
He's going to attack.

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:23.820
If you lose Cyberse Wizard, you'll lose.

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:24.950
I know.

00:13:25.420 --> 00:13:29.690
Since I control Cracking Dragon, 
I'm the strongest duelist!

00:13:29.900 --> 00:13:30.940
Battle!

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:33.620
Traffic Blast!

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:37.400
I activate the trap, Three Strikes Barrier!

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:45.540
I choose that my monster won't 
be destroyed in battle this turn!

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:52.510
But you still take damage.

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:54.450
To the right, Playmaker!

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:02.650
This match is over.

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:05.720
No.  I still have life points.

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:12.180
It seems you don't understand what I meant.

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:26.280
The Data Storm will swallow 
you.  You're terminated.

00:14:31.880 --> 00:14:33.550
Playmaker!

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:37.980
Yusaku!

00:15:08.020 --> 00:15:11.590
You led me here on purpose, didn't you.

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:12.960
You knew?

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:16.330
And why you didn't tell me about Skills!

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:17.710
Yeah, that's right.

00:15:17.710 --> 00:15:22.300
Because this Data Storm is your 
only chance to defeat him.

00:15:22.690 --> 00:15:24.040
What do you mean?

00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:28.010
Never-before-seen monsters 
live inside this Data Storm.

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:30.060
Never-before-seen monsters?

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:34.250
The more intense the Data Storm, 
the more powerful the monster!

00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:38.820
Now's the time to use 
your Skill, Storm Access!

00:15:39.220 --> 00:15:42.080
There's no other way for us to survive!

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:47.560
When you have 1000 or fewer LP...

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:51.520
...Storm Access lets you access 
one random card in the Data Storm!

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:54.470
Seize the wind, Playmaker!

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:11.320
Hang in there, Playmaker!

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:23.900
There are three reasons 
why I must win this duel.

00:16:25.010 --> 00:16:30.150
#1: To regain the moments I've lost!

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:35.840
#2: To rescue Kusanagi's younger 
brother from the darkness!

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:40.710
#3: To meet the one who gave me courage!

00:16:41.260 --> 00:16:42.460
You!

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:49.680
Now!

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:51.800
Storm Access!

00:17:02.440 --> 00:17:06.370
What?  The Data Storm 
should've swallowed you up!

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:09.140
The match isn't over yet!

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:11.710
My turn!  I draw!

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:15.350
I activate Cyberse Wizard's effect.

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:18.250
Cyberse Algorithm!

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:23.760
Die already!

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:26.060
It's pointless!  I activate my trap!

00:17:26.300 --> 00:17:27.760
Pulse Mines!

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:31.950
All your monsters switch to defense position!

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:34.800
Calm down.

00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:37.490
I summon Stack Reviver.

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:42.020
No matter what monster you summon...

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:44.920
...Pulse Mines will switch 
it to defense position.

00:17:48.220 --> 00:17:53.220
You fool.  You don't understand 
Cracking Dragon's power.

00:17:53.220 --> 00:17:55.190
You have 400 LP.

00:17:55.540 --> 00:17:58.670
And the damage you'll take is also 400!

00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:00.120
Crack Fall!

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:03.330
This is the end.

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:08.800
He survived?  Impossible!

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:10.300
What's wrong?

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:14.540
You're the one who doesn't understand 
Cracking Dragon's power.

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:19.710
Its effect lowers my LP equal 
to the decrease in ATK.

00:18:19.710 --> 00:18:23.010
Stack Reviver's original ATK is 100.

00:18:23.420 --> 00:18:28.820
It lost 100 ATK, so I only lost 100 LP.

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:34.130
You strengthened your defenses, 
knowing you'd take damage.

00:18:34.130 --> 00:18:36.640
I'm no amateur duelist!

00:18:36.940 --> 00:18:41.100
From my hand, I activate the 
spell card, <i>Effect Cowl</i>.

00:18:42.280 --> 00:18:47.440
When there's a Cyberse on my field, 
I don't take effect damage this turn.

00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:50.770
I activate the trap, Cyberse Beacon!

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:53.650
Since I took damage this turn...

00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:57.780
...I can add one Level 4 or lower 
Cyberse in my deck to my hand.

00:18:58.120 --> 00:19:01.650
I Special Summon Backup Secretary!

00:19:03.840 --> 00:19:09.660
When there's a Cyberse on my field, I can 
Special Summon this card from my hand.

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:12.100
Keep gathering those weaklings.

00:19:12.100 --> 00:19:14.500
They're no match for Cracking Dragon!

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:16.240
Are you sure?

00:19:16.240 --> 00:19:18.840
I'm going to play my secret weapon!

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:20.350
Secret weapon?

00:19:20.350 --> 00:19:21.750
You make me laugh.

00:19:21.750 --> 00:19:26.310
No matter what you play, as long as I have 
Cracking Dragon and Pulse Mines's effects-

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:27.550
It can't be!

00:19:27.910 --> 00:19:28.910
Appear!

00:19:30.410 --> 00:19:32.640
The circuit that leads to the future!

00:19:44.980 --> 00:19:46.640
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:19:46.640 --> 00:19:50.130
I need at least two Effect 
Monsters to summon!

00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:56.540
I set Stack Reviver, Cyberse Wizard and 
Backup Secretary in the Link Markers.

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:02.040
Circuit combine!

00:20:03.770 --> 00:20:08.850
Link Summon!  Appear, Link 3 Decode Talker!

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:27.440
Monsters from the Extra Deck are Special 
Summoned to the Extra Monster Zone.

00:20:28.550 --> 00:20:31.810
Your secret weapon is a Link Monster?

00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:36.840
You drew a card using Storm Access 
and instantly mastered it.

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:39.120
Impressive, Playmaker.

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:42.090
Link Monsters don't have Levels!

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:44.330
And can't be switched to defense position!

00:20:44.330 --> 00:20:51.760
In other words, Cracking Dragon and Pulse 
Mines's effects don't work against Decode Talker!

00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:56.530
I activate Stack Reviver's 
effect from my graveyard!

00:20:56.740 --> 00:21:01.020
It lets me Special Summon Cyberse 
Wizard in defense position.

00:21:04.980 --> 00:21:09.480
Decode Talker gains 500 ATK for every Link.

00:21:10.050 --> 00:21:12.220
Power Integration!

00:21:15.440 --> 00:21:18.660
3300 ATK?

00:21:19.390 --> 00:21:21.400
Go, Decode Talker!

00:21:22.020 --> 00:21:24.010
Cyberse Wizard's effect!

00:21:24.280 --> 00:21:29.600
Decode Talker can now deal piercing damage!

00:21:30.160 --> 00:21:33.040
Decode End!

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:39.980
But Cracking Dragon can't be 
destroyed by a lower Level monster-

00:21:41.220 --> 00:21:44.720
Link Monsters don't have Levels!

00:21:57.060 --> 00:22:00.530
You have no right to call yourself a duelist!

00:22:23.740 --> 00:22:26.750
